From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:48:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: memory callbacks before the access

QEMU_PLUGIN_MEM_BEFORE and QEMU_PLUGIN_MEM_AFTER are or-ed into a memory
callback registration; qemu_plugin_mem_is_before() tells them apart. A
registration without either is after-only, as before, so existing plugins
see no new calls.

Before a load the value is not known; before a store it is (stores now put
their value in plugin_mem_value ahead of the access, which the after event
reuses, so nothing more runs per access). Atomics get a read and a write
before event from atomic_mmu_lookup, without a value. 128-bit TCG accesses
have no before events yet.

From aking's before/after memory callbacks on panda-re/qemu wrapup-rebase
(25af52e0, 6539fa00, 303df341, 858992b9), reworked: the phase is a flag that
defaults to after rather than a new meaning for MEM_R/W, so plugins that do
not ask for it are not called twice.
---
 accel/tcg/cputlb.c            |  7 +++++++
 accel/tcg/ldst_common.c.inc   | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 accel/tcg/plugin-gen.c        |  8 +++-----
 include/plugins/qemu-plugin.h | 20 ++++++++++++++++++
 include/qemu/plugin.h         | 14 +++++++++++++
 plugins/api.c                 |  5 +++++
 plugins/core.c                |  4 ++--
 tcg/tcg-op-ldst.c             | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 8 files changed, 103 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/accel/tcg/cputlb.c b/accel/tcg/cputlb.c
index d7f51c94c29454c80b54d56252c73035e73747e8..f1ba05a5c0efc8421864b511fe0f95601025411c 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/cputlb.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/cputlb.c
@@ -1910,6 +1910,13 @@ static void *atomic_mmu_lookup(CPUState *cpu, vaddr addr, MemOpIdx oi,
                              full->attrs, wp_flags, retaddr);
     }
 
+    if (cpu_plugin_mem_cbs_enabled(cpu)) {
+        qemu_plugin_vcpu_mem_cb(cpu, addr, 0, 0, oi,
+                                QEMU_PLUGIN_MEM_R | QEMU_PLUGIN_MEM_BEFORE);
+        qemu_plugin_vcpu_mem_cb(cpu, addr, 0, 0, oi,
+                                QEMU_PLUGIN_MEM_W | QEMU_PLUGIN_MEM_BEFORE);
+    }
+
     return hostaddr;
 
  stop_the_world:
